{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Blessed is Adonai</b> — one praises HaShem that He strengthened His hand." "<b>Who bears for us</b> — His blessings. And some say: for the verb-stem is our salvation, and the El will be on account of El for salvation[s]; to us the El, to us He alone is for salvation[s], and He has outlets and means to put our enemies to death."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 68, :notes {1 "The text of this comment is dense and elliptical; 'תוצאות וסבות' rendered hyper-literally as 'outlets and means.' The phrase 'אל למושעות' (El for salvation[s]) is repeated with the plural suffix, reflecting Ibn Ezra's grammatical argument about the noun pattern."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:12.087521015Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}